WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.050
Your body is made up of over 200 bones,

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:07.610
a few trillion microbes, and
as many as 37 trillion cells.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.269
And while death is often thought of as

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:11.442
the end of the line for your self,

00:00:11.442 --> 00:00:14.083
your body still has a long way to go.

00:00:17.592 --> 00:00:19.430
It doesn't take long before your body

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.800
starts to lose what makes you you.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.180
Just a few minutes after death,

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.790
one of the first things
to go is your brain.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.190
You see, when your heart stops beating,

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.210
it halts blood flow, which
is supposed to transport

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.480
oxygen to your organs and tissues.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.970
So without blood, the most active,

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.100
oxygen-guzzling organs
and tissues go first.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.425
And the results are...moist.

00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:46.842
Because the cells that make
up those organs and tissues

00:00:46.842 --> 00:00:48.538
are 70% water.

00:00:48.538 --> 00:00:50.672
Without oxygen to keep them alive,

00:00:50.672 --> 00:00:52.690
the cells self-destruct,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.040
spilling all that fluid
onto the coffin floor.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.280
By that night, an even more
troubling process begins

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.580
in the gut.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.090
Your dying immune system
can no longer contain

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.480
the trillions of hungry
microbes that normally

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.400
help digest the food you eat.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.780
So they escape.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.040
First, they travel from
the lower intestines

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.730
through your tissues, veins, and arteries.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:19.290
Within hours, they reach
your liver and gallbladder,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.400
which contain a
yellow-green bile meant for

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.210
breaking down fat when you're alive.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.550
But after the microbes are
through eating those organs,

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.920
that bile starts to flood the body,

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.100
staining it a yellow-green.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.120
From about day two to four,
the microbes are everywhere.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.240
And they're producing toxic gases,

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.080
like ammonia and hydrogen sulfide,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.540
which will expand and cause your body

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.700
to not only bloat, but stink.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.690
After three or four months,

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.120
your yellow-green complexion
has turned brownish-black

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.520
because your blood
vessels have deteriorated

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.737
to the point that the iron
inside them spills out,

00:01:57.737 --> 00:02:00.580
becoming brownish-black as it oxidizes.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.240
Also around this time,

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.536
the molecular structures that

00:02:03.536 --> 00:02:06.150
hold your cells together break away,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.290
so your tissues collapse
into a watery mush.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.800
And in a little over a year,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.770
your cotton clothes disintegrate,

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:18.660
as acidic body fluids and
toxins break them down.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.984
Only the nylon seams
and waistband survive.

00:02:21.984 --> 00:02:26.080
At this point, nothing
dramatic happens for a while.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.379
But by a decade in, given enough moisture,

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:32.750
the wet, low-oxygen environment

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.840
sets off a chemical reaction

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.100
that turns the fat in your thighs and butt

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:41.160
to a soap-like substance called grave wax.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.810
On the other hand, drier
conditions lead to mummification.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.660
That's right, you can mummify naturally.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.450
No wrappings, chemicals,

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.640
or intimidating instruments required.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.540
Because throughout this
entire decomposition process,

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.890
water is evaporating through the thin skin

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:03.100
on your ears, nose, and
eyelids, causing them to dry

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:07.090
out and turn black, aka mummify.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.330
By 50 years in, your
tissues will have liquefied

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:15.259
and disappeared, leaving behind
mummified skin and tendons.

00:03:15.259 --> 00:03:17.540
Eventually these too will disintegrate,

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.655
and after 80 years in that coffin,

00:03:20.655 --> 00:03:23.700
your bones will crack as the soft collagen

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.530
inside them deteriorates,

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.787
leaving nothing but the
brittle mineral frame behind.

00:03:28.787 --> 00:03:31.639
But even that shell won't last forever.

00:03:31.639 --> 00:03:34.140
A century in, the last of your bones

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.460
will have collapsed into dust.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.970
And only the most durable
part of your body,

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.561
your teeth, will remain.

00:03:41.561 --> 00:03:45.383
Teeth, grave wax, and some nylon threads.

